From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Manuel Arto <manuel.arto@nethermind.io>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:42:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] feat(daisugi): check the Daisugi block hash with the
 EIP-8288 commitment

Replaces the skipped optimistic-sync block-hash check with an independent
derivation: the dependency hash is computed from the payload's frame
transactions the way the Nethermind prototype does (DEP_VERIFY triples,
zero data hashes resolved to the EIP-8141 signature hash, canonical order,
BLAKE2s with the leanSTARK domain split), then appended with
keccak(starkProof) after the empty BAL and zero slot placeholders.
An undecodable frame transaction fails the check.

Vectors in daisugi_block_hash.rs were emitted by Nethermind.
